  "id": "DrugBank_DB01167 - MONDO_1648",
  "verbalization": "Itraconazole is implicated in the pathogenesis of Esophageal Candidiasis through a multi-step pathway involving fungal infections. The evidence suggests that Itraconazole is linked to Candidemia, a systemic fungal infection, which in turn is associated with Esophageal Candidiasis. This indicates that Itraconazole may have a role in the treatment or prevention of fungal infections that lead to esophageal candidiasis. The indirect relationship is supported by the presence of multiple pathways where Itraconazole is indicated for fungal infections that ultimately result in Esophageal Candidiasis. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential of Itraconazole to influence fungal infections at various stages, suggesting a broader therapeutic or prophylactic role in the context of esophageal candidiasis.",
